+- O(n) linear scan
+- O(n log n) sorting, binary search
+- O(n^2) nested loops (if n < 5000)
+- Polynomial-time DP
+- Greedy algorithms
+- Segment trees, Fenwick trees
+
+### Forbidden in solution.py:
+- O(n!) permutation enumeration
+- O(2^n) subset enumeration
+- BFS/Dijkstra over state-space with > 100 states
+- O(n^3) or higher (unless n very small)
+
+### Allowed ONLY in brute.py:
+- Exponential algorithms (for n ≤ 6)
+- itertools.permutations
+- Recursive backtracking
+- Exhaustive search
+
+---
+
+## Key Design Decisions
+
+1. **No stdin file redirection**: Used `subprocess.run(input=...)` instead of temp files for cleaner, more portable code
+2. **Raw error output**: Agents receive raw stderr/stdout without parsing; they can analyze contextually
+3. **Bounded iteration**: `range(3)` ensures at most 3 redesign cycles before requiring human help
+4. **Two-tier gates**: Complexity gate blocks bad algorithms early, final gate catches timing issues
+5. **Pattern discovery**: Step 5.5 guides formula inference for optimization problems
+
